       "   {'key': ' Once upon a time, in a land called Ukraine, there was a popular news website called Ukrayinska Pravda. This website was started by a kind man named Georgiy Gongadze who loved sharing stories about his country\\'s national politics. The website was written mostly in Ukrainian, but sometimes it had special articles in Russian too!\\n\\nOne day, two friends, Maria and Ivan, decided to explore the website together. They saw pictures of people talking and writing things down. Maria asked, \"What are those people doing?\" Ivan replied, \"They are journalists. They write news stories to share with everyone.\" Maria then wondered, \"Why do they need to write in different languages?\" Ivan explained, \"That way, more people can understand what they\\'re saying!\"\\n\\nAs Maria and Ivan kept looking around, they found an article about something called \\'dowry.\\' It said that when someone gets married, they might ask for gifts or money from the other person\\'s family. Sometimes this made some parents go into debt, even having trouble paying bills like buying food and toys! Maria felt sad hearing this. She asked, \"But why would anyone want so much stuff just for getting married?\"\\n\\nIvan thought for a moment and answered, \"Well, long ago, giving gifts showed how much you cared for the person you were marrying. But now, some people take advantage of that idea and expect too much. That\\'s not fair or nice.\" Maria nodded and agreed, \"Yes, we should always be fair and think about others\\' feelings.\"\\n\\nLater that day, Maria and Ivan played pretend wedding, remembering to only ask for small, meaningful gifts instead of expecting too much. And whenever they read Ukrayinska Pravda, they learned more about Ukraine and its people, spreading kindness and understanding through their little community.\\n\\nIn short, here\\'s your story:\\n\\nThere\\'s a site called Ukrayinska Pravda where people share news about Ukraine. Two pals, Maria and Ivan, discovered that folks once gave presents during marriage. However, occasionally, asking for plenty of items may cause problems. So, let us remember to be type and reasonable when playing pretend weddings and learning new things!',\n",
